    "updated_at": "2025-11-14T06:42:05Z",
    "body": "Related: https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10879\n\nIf it's compatible to change the parsing of `noscript`, I think it would be good to switch on \"user has scripting enabled in the browser\" for `noscript` parsing and UA stylesheet. This should address the XSS attacks with `noscript`, but keep the utility for users who have turned off scripting.\n\n> E.g., I'm pretty sure it was fairly recently that we did the work around sandboxing and that making that work the same as scripting being disabled was an intentional design choice.\n\n@annevk do you have a pointer? I tried to find a relevant change by looking at blame and searching PRs but didn't find where this was changed.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
